From: Matthew Dowell <mbd06b+github@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:12:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(brit-cli): narrow the read-only list; flush stdout
 before the status

Review of 8e5072ffd..1cceb1264:

- Off the list, each with its reason beside it: `is-clean`, `is-changed`
  (predicates whose answer is their status, and their status engine can
  run a clean filter); `commit describe`, `submodule list`
  (`--dirty-suffix` runs that engine); `remote refs`, `remote ref-map`
  (a credential helper may store or erase a credential, and helper or
  askpass output bypasses the watched writer; `ls-remote` has the same
  property and is left for the brit session to decide alike). Bare
  `submodule` stays. 26 paths remain admitted by this lane.
- For a read-only command, stdout is flushed through the watched writer
  after `run()` and before `exit_status()` reads `closed_reader::seen()`,
  so a short newline-free blob or `[]` meets a closed reader in time.
- The `attributes validate-baseline` reason is corrected, and the known
  limits (raw `--trace`/progress stderr; a streaming query stops at its
  first failed write) are recorded beside the list.

Journey: rows for the removed paths dropped; new rows for `show HEAD:nonl`
(short blob, no newline), `-f json revision previous-branches` (`[]`),
`tree info no-such-revision` with stderr closed (own status), and
closed-stderr `tree info` / `mailmap entries`; `fsck`'s live status is
asserted. On 1cceb1264 the blob and `[]` rows exit 0 and the `tree info`
failure row exits 141.

